.TH CHTTPSVR_REGISTER_STREAMING_HANDLER 3 "2026-10-01" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler \- register a streaming handler on the root router
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_register_streaming_handler(chttpsvr srv,
                                  chttp_method_t method,
                                  const char *pattern,
                                  chttpsvr_handler_fn fn, void *ctx);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function works like chttpsvr_register_handler, but it marks the
route as a streaming route.  chttpsvr_req_read is therefore available
to the handler, and the handler reads the body one piece at a time.
chttpsvr_req_read returns -1 on a route that is not a streaming route.

A streaming handler reads its body at the pace of the client, so it can
hold its thread for as long as the client takes.  It therefore runs on
a pool of its own, of chttpsvr_config_t.streaming_thread_count
threads, and never on the reactor thread or on the worker pool that
serves buffered routes.  Slow streaming clients can occupy at most that
pool.  The server creates the pool at the first streaming request that
it receives.  The thread counts as a worker of its server: a call that
a handler must not make on its own server, such as chttpsvr_destroy()
or a restart, is refused or fatal there exactly as it is in a buffered
handler.  chttpsvr_config_t.streaming_thread_count set to
CHTTPSVR_STREAMING_POOL_OFF runs streaming handlers on the worker pool
instead; chttpsvr_start(3) describes what that changes.

You can use CHTTP_ANY for method to match every HTTP method on the
pattern.  See chttpsvr_register_handler for the full rules of
CHTTP_ANY.

The server routes the request as soon as it parses the headers, and
before it reads any body byte.  The worker therefore reads the body
itself, batch by batch, directly off the socket.  The reactor thread
never reads it.  chttpsvr_req_read gives each batch to the handler as
it arrives.  It returns 0 after the body ends, and every later call
also returns 0, so the EOF is idempotent.  It returns -1 for a
connection that dropped, for a body above max_body_size, and for a
client that stalled.  chttpsvr_config_t.stream_read_timeout_us bounds
each gap, and chttpsvr_config_t.max_body_read_duration_us bounds the
whole read when you set it.  Call chttpsvr_req_stream_error to tell
these causes apart.  chttpsvr_config_t.min_transfer_rate_bps also ends
the read of a client whose average rate falls below that floor, with
ccol_timed_out.

A streaming request that finds every streaming thread busy waits, with
no thread, in a queue of chttpsvr_config_t.streaming_queue_capacity
entries.  The server answers with 503 Service Unavailable and
"Retry-After: 5" immediately when that queue is full, and when a
request waits there longer than
chttpsvr_config_t.streaming_queue_timeout_us.  The handler never runs
for such a request.  None of this blocks the reactor thread.

The pattern rules of chttpsvr_register_handler apply here too.
pattern must start with '/'.  The library rejects a pattern with two
slashes together, and one with a slash at the end.  A {name} segment
must hold only [A-Za-z0-9_].  The same {name} must not appear more
than once in one pattern.  See chttpsvr_register_handler for the full
details of the pattern checks, and for the rules of the decoding of a
path segment.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args when srv is CHTTPSVR_INVALID, or a stale handle that
                  something already destroyed; when pattern or fn is
                  NULL; when pattern does not start with '/'; when
                  pattern has two slashes together or a slash at the
                  end; when a {name} segment has a character outside
                  [A-Za-z0-9_]; or when the same {name} appears more
                  than once.
ccol_not_enough_memory when an allocation fails.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_register_handler (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_read (3),
.BR CHTTPSVR_CONFIG_DEFAULT (3)
